artner]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1844014049761083394/Qn5KhYCl_200x200.jpg"></p><p>Luke Burgis (@lukeburgis) on X</p><p>I’m looking for a key partner to build the Cluny Institute with. A new full-time position in Washington, DC is now open for applications. The Director of Operations &amp; Strategy will work closely with me and our core team to create and build things that invite the spirit to</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/lukeburgis/status/1986481709341360235">https://x.com/lukeburgis/status/1986481709341360235</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/11/friday-assorted-links-546.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=friday-assorted-links-546">Friday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/lukeburgis/status/1986481709341360235</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/lukeburgis/status/1986481709341360235</guid><pubDate>Fri, 07 Nov 2025 16:30:08 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Sam Altman on the role of government in AI]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1904933748015255552/k43GMz63_200x200.jpg"></p><p>Sam Altman (@sama) on X</p><p>I would like to clarify a few things. First, the obvious one: we do not have or want government guarantees for OpenAI datacenters. We believe that governments should not pick winners or losers, and that taxpayers should not bail out companies that make bad business decisions or</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/sama/status/1986514377470845007">https://x.com/sama/status/1986514377470845007</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/11/friday-assorted-links-546.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=friday-assorted-links-546">Friday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/sama/status/1986514377470845007</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/sama/status/1986514377470845007</guid><pub